From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SunUEFI source preparation <source-preparation@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 07 Oct 2026 22:21:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(leds): correct qcom flash cleanup indexing

leds_count is the number of successfully registered LED entries.  The
cleanup and remove loops currently index this count before decrementing it.
After all child LEDs have registered, that accesses one element beyond the
allocated v4l2_flash array.

Check the count first, decrement it before indexing, and release every
registered slot.  Do not terminate cleanup on a NULL slot: torch-only LEDs
and configurations without the V4L2 wrapper may leave NULL entries, which
v4l2_flash_release() already accepts.
---
 drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c b/drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c
index b03a6833e3e3..c2fefeec9b80 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/flash/leds-qcom-flash.c
@@ -953,8 +953,8 @@
 
 	return regmap_field_write(flash_data->r_fields[REG_TORCH_CLAMP], flash_data->torch_clamp);
 release:
-	while (flash_data->v4l2_flash[flash_data->leds_count] && flash_data->leds_count)
-		v4l2_flash_release(flash_data->v4l2_flash[flash_data->leds_count--]);
+	while (flash_data->leds_count)
+		v4l2_flash_release(flash_data->v4l2_flash[--flash_data->leds_count]);
 	return rc;
 }
 
@@ -962,8 +962,8 @@
 {
 	struct qcom_flash_data *flash_data = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
-	while (flash_data->v4l2_flash[flash_data->leds_count] && flash_data->leds_count)
-		v4l2_flash_release(flash_data->v4l2_flash[flash_data->leds_count--]);
+	while (flash_data->leds_count)
+		v4l2_flash_release(flash_data->v4l2_flash[--flash_data->leds_count]);
 
 	mutex_destroy(&flash_data->lock);
 }
